      "observation": "The integral measures total conserved quantity between the endpoints, and its change is accounted for solely by endpoint flux."
    },
    {
      "location": "Raw PDF page 26, printed page 4, Section 1.1.1, first explanatory paragraph",
      "anchor": "the conservation law must also contain source terms",
      "observation": "The text distinguishes the displayed conservation law from models with production or loss, such as chemical reactions, which require source terms."
    },
