      "The discussion concerns solutions of conservation laws with the integral balance (1.10), whose components represent conserved densities. It does not assert this balance for an arbitrary discontinuous function. [Printed p. 4, Section 1.1.1, (1.10) and its explanatory paragraph; printed p. 5, Section 1.1.2, reference to shock-solutions to conservation laws.]",
      "For the stated derivation of differential equation (1.8) from integral equation (1.10), q and f(q) must be sufficiently smooth. This qualification belongs to the derivation, not to the assertion that the integral formulation accommodates discontinuities. [Printed p. 4, Section 1.1.2, first paragraph.]",
